<title>BELGIUM: Powerfin H1 '96 net profit down 5.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Powerfin H1 '96 net profit down 5.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30. (figures in billions of Belgian francs)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			4.33   vs   4.58</p>
<p>    Group net per share in francs     181    vs   191.2</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items		   0.003  vs   0.018</p>
<p>    Gross operating profit		5.71   vs   5.65</p>
<p>    Taxation				  1.38   vs   1.09</p>
<p>NOTE - Powerfin SA is a Belgian utilities holding firm whose main asset is a stake in utility holding group Electrabel SA. Powerfin said in a statement accompanying the results it expected to pay a dividend on 1996 full year earnings at least equal to that on 1995.</p>
<p>Powerfin said that since the start of the year the group has pursued electricity and gas investments in Chile, Thailand, Singapore, the United States, Kazakhstan and China.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
